thod'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 7]}, 'Convolution layers': {'description': ['Layers within a Convolutional Neural Network that perform the majority of the computation (FLOPS).', 'Layers within a CNN that perform convolution operations, targeted for optimization in sparse CNNs.', 'Layers where a bulk of computation belongs to.', 'Layers within a CNN that perform convolutional operations.', 'Layers in a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) that perform convolution operations. The text specifically mentions conv1 and conv2, highlighting their varying degrees of sparsifiability.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 5, 6, 7]}, 'Sparse convolution': {'description': ['A technique used in sparse CNNs to reduce compute requirements by applying sparsity to convolution operations.', 'A convolutional technique that exploits sparsity in weight tensors to potentially achieve computational speedups.', 'A technique used to speed up CNNs by reducing computations.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 4, 5]}, 'Classification speed': {'description': ['The speed at which a CNN can classify inputs, a key performance metric targeted for improvement in sparse CNN research.', 'The objective of accelerating the speed of image classification in CNNs.', 'The objective of achieving high classification speed, specifically measured in images per second.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 7]}, 'Model size reduction': {'description': ['The objective of reducing the number of parameters in a CNN model, often achieved through sparsification or compression techniques.', 'The objective of decreasing the size of a model.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 4]}, 'Arithmetic intensity': {'description': ['A measure of the ratio of computation to data movement, relevant to the efficiency of sparse convolution.', 'The ratio of arithmetic operations to memory accesses, used to characterize the computational efficiency of the direct sparse convolution algorithm.'], 'type': ['method', 'task'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 4]}, 'Limitation to large filters': {'description': ['Some prior sparse convolution methods are only applicable to large filters (e.g., 9x9), which limits their usage for modern CNNs where small filters (e.g., 3x3) are popular.', 'A challenge where some sparse convolution methods are only applicable to large filters (e.g., 9x9), limiting their use in modern CNNs that often use small filters (e.g., 3x3).'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Research Thrusts on Sparse CNNs': {'description': ['The area of research focused on improving sparse CNNs, specifically targeting convolution layers to enhance classification speed.', 'Convolutional Neural Networks that utilize sparse methods to improve efficiency.'], 'type': ['method', 'task'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 7]}, 'direct sparse convolution algorithm': {'description': ['An algorithm presented to advance the state-of-the-art in sparse convolution for speeding up CNNs.', 'A specific algorithm introduced in the text for speeding up CNNs by performing sparse convolution directly.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'convolution layers': {'description': ['Layers within a CNN that perform convolution operations.', 'Layers in a CNN that perform convolution operations.', 'Layers in a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) that perform convolution operations. The text specifically mentions conv1 and conv2, highlighting their varying degrees of sparsifiability.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 6]}, 'fully connected layers': {'description': ['Layers within a CNN that are fully connected.', "Layers in a CNN where each neuron is connected to all neurons in the previous layer. The text refers to these as 'fc' layers and discusses their sparsity in relation to regularization parameters."], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 6]}, 'accuracy': {'description': ["The correctness of the model's predictions.", 'The objective